  <question type="multianswer">
    <name><text>MB6 - Set operations on explicit sets (Cloze)</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>[Operations on Sets]</strong> Let \( A = \{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\} \) and \( B = \{2, 4, 6, 8\} \).</p>
<p>(a) The intersection \( A \cap B \) is {1:MULTICHOICE:=&#123;2, 4&#125;~&#123;2, 4, 6, 8&#125;~&#123;1, 3, 5&#125;~&#123;6, 8&#125;}.</p>
<p>(b) The number of elements in \( A \cup B \) is {2:NUMERICAL:=7:0}.</p>
<p>(c) The number of elements in \( A \setminus B \) (in \(A\) but not in \(B\)) is {1:NUMERICAL:=3:0}.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Common elements: \(\{2,4\}\). (b) \( A \cup B = \{1,2,3,4,5,6,8\} \Rightarrow 7 \). (c) \( A\setminus B = \{1,3,5\} \Rightarrow 3 \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
  </question>

  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>MB7 - Relations: the order relation =&gt; on integers</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>[Relations]</strong> Define \(R\) on \( \mathbb{Z} \) by \( a\,R\,b \iff a \ge b \). Select <em>all</em> properties \(R\) has.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\(a\ge a\) (reflexive); if \(a\ge b\) and \(b\ge a\) then \(a=b\) (antisymmetric); transitivity holds. So \(\ge\) is a partial order — <em>not</em> symmetric.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>false</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <correctfeedback format="html"><text>Correct.</text></correctfeedback>
    <partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text>Partially correct.</text></partiallycorrectfeedback>
    <incorrectfeedback format="html"><text>Incorrect.</text></incorrectfeedback>
    <answer fraction="33.33333" format="html"><text>Reflexive</text><feedback format="html"><text>Yes.</text></feedback></answer>
    <answer fraction="-100" format="html"><text>Symmetric</text><feedback format="html"><text>No — \(3\ge 2\) but \(2\not\ge 3\).</text></feedback></answer>
    <answer fraction="33.33333" format="html"><text>Antisymmetric</text><feedback format="html"><text>Yes.</text></feedback></answer>
    <answer fraction="33.33333" format="html"><text>Transitive</text><feedback format="html"><text>Yes.</text></feedback></answer>
  </question>

  <question type="shortanswer">
    <name><text>MB8 - Functions: classify f(x)=x^3</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>[Functions]</strong> Consider \( f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R},\ f(x)=x^3 \). In one word, give the strongest correct term (injective, surjective, or bijective).</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\(x^3\) is strictly increasing and takes every real value, so it is one-to-one and onto: <strong>bijective</strong>, with inverse \(f^{-1}(y)=\sqrt[3]{y}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <usecase>0</usecase>
    <answer fraction="100" format="moodle_auto_format"><text>bijective</text><feedback format="html"><text>Correct.</text></feedback></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="moodle_auto_format"><text>bijection</text><feedback format="html"><text>Correct.</text></feedback></answer>
    <answer fraction="50" format="moodle_auto_format"><text>injective</text><feedback format="html"><text>True, but it is also surjective — bijective is strongest.</text></feedback></answer>
  </question>

